Under the reset-diverse screen the deployed policy family reached
$98.0$--$98.2\%$ three-lap success at $18.32$--$18.34$\,s
($\sigma = 0.41$--$0.48$\,s). Under the deployment-matched ground-only
protocol (Table~\ref{tab:groundonly}) the selected checkpoint reached $100\%$
success at $18.10$\,s with $\sigma = 0.08$\,s. The variance collapse between
protocols is expected and is itself a useful diagnostic: nearly all of the
reset-diverse variance comes from start-state diversity rather than from
dynamics.

\subsection{Speed candidates}

\begin{table*}[t]
